title: Home
description: Kyle Hubbard is a Solutions Architect on TrendAI's Global Alliances team, working the AWS partnership and the question of how customers govern AI agents in production.
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="mono-label hero__eyebrow">TrendAI &times; AWS &middot; Global Alliances</p>
    <h1 class="hero__title">
      Every partnership has two sides.
      <span class="hero__title-b">I work in the space between them.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero__lede">
      I'm Kyle Hubbard. I own the technical side of TrendAI's AWS partnership &mdash; the
      positioning, the roadmap conversations, and the executive narrative in both
      directions. The subject most of that turns on right now is AI security: how a customer
      governs an agent once it's in production, what it can act on, and where a person stays
      in the loop.
    </p>
    <p class="hero__actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/partnerships/">The alliance work</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/resume/">Resume</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--ruled">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">What the<br />seat covers</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lede band__lede">
        An alliance isn't a set of tasks, it's a book of business with a technical spine.
        Four things sit on my desk.
      </p>

      <div class="scopelist">
        {% for item in scope %}
        <div class="scope">
          <p class="mono-label scope__label">{{ item.label }}</p>
          <p class="scope__text">{{ item.text }}</p>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--ruled">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">Translating<br />both directions</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="lede band__lede">
        The useful thing I do isn't picking a side. It's saying the same true thing twice, so
        the people building it and the people funding it are actually agreeing.
      </p>

      <div class="registers">
        {% for item in highlights %}
        <div class="register">
          <p class="mono-label register__topic">{{ item.topic }}</p>
          <div class="register__side">
            <p class="mono-label register__label">{{ item.left.label }}</p>
            <p class="register__text">{{ item.left.text }}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="register__side register__side--b">
            <p class="mono-label register__label">{{ item.right.label }}</p>
            <p class="register__text">{{ item.right.text }}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--ruled">
  <div class="wrap band__grid">
    <div class="rail">
      <p class="mono-label">How I got here</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Eleven years of my career have been spent working across an organizational boundary
        rather than inside one &mdash; state agencies at Fast Enterprises, 73 enterprise
        security deployments at Black Duck, and now hyperscaler partnerships at TrendAI. The
        constant is being the person both sides can ask a direct question and get a straight
        answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/about/">More on that</a> &middot; <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
